  "reasoning": "The product contains a fused quinazoline heterocycle and a chiral oxazolidinone side chain. The 'Heterocycle formation' context indicates the cyclization step that constructs the quinazoline core. This transformation is classically achieved via the condensation of a 2-aminobenzonitrile with an aldehyde or ketone. Retrosynthetically, disconnecting the C2–N1 and C4–N3 bonds of the quinazoline ring reveals a 2-amino-5-arylbenzonitrile precursor and acetaldehyde (which provides the methyl group at the C4 position). The chiral oxazolidinone moiety remains intact as a spectator substituent on the aryl ring throughout the cyclization. Therefore, the most logical precursors are the corresponding 2-amino-arylbenzonitrile and acetaldehyde.",
  "final_answer": "N#Cc1ccc(c2ccc([C@H](C)N3CC[C@](CC(C)(C)O)(c4ccccc4)OC3=O)cc2)cc1N.CC=O"
